uuid "d8df5920-44fd-5cbe-9f0a-2111cda02c34" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} {:answer/id #uuid "762ae4d9-bf4c-5ca6-bb90-84a859083154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2facf3b-7a9b-53cc-9a3f-b2a9bf7a9c24" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468533}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "101d0c36-a705-552a-b14b-442022f64eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-48734" :question/problem "![](images/14/14fdc374842064ad40ebbadf3dab16191ecfdeec8c416b4e7f17beffce44fb40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$” is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=3.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(3)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$” is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the derivative is undefined at $x=3$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$” is false. The function does not have a local maximum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for $x$ close enough  to the point $x=3,$ so,  actually,  $f(x)$ has local minimum at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, only statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$” is true." :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186729513 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329920} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 88.80199999999999 :task-item/id #uuid "55cda11c-e7b4-478d-911f-a2cd7dcdfb84" :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467621} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467622} {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624}] :task-item/status {:db/ident :task-item.status/correct} :task-item/working-ended-at #inst "2026-10-28T16:46:15.789Z"}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1f3def-98d2-524a-b778-f7e66a7f3296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467626} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fbad27-f24f-5ab5-9dc2-2649e548b79d" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956e3925-042a-5383-b9cd-d81e8467a088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467628} {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629} :answer-field/id #uuid "98dade12-9621-5587-bfac-2f8ef6ab2b14" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b46b1cc-def4-5734-bd89-8f1d5131c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467630} {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e72066-eadb-5611-801e-ce8cccffd34f" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468536}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5dfd5ad-23a9-54fc-83bf-a64cab147aed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48737" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a2298a8255a86c803560793658593a22f7f77590ef350c1e0cebd974fce7750.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$” is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2$ since $f(2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=2.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$” is true. The graph of the function has a sharp edge (corner) at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)$ does not exist. Hence, $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, all statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Critical and Stationary Points of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b45765bb-4323-55a3-9da0-49d29c7b3298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730133} {:answer/id #uuid "26ce43ba-b52e-5747-902f-02f7b7cb9f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b45765bb-4323-55a3-9da0-49d29c7b3298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730133} :answer-field/id #uuid "196c7fc1-9563-53fc-af52-ba7e8ad3497c" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85473738-96cb-5b97-86b1-95c79d4be94f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730135} {:answer/id #uuid "b2cfde65-7b18-598a-9f73-dea35da8814b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2cfde65-7b18-598a-9f73-dea35da8814b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730136} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0aed0c-cc12-5d19-a281-108400541791" :answer-field/key "$x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31691bca-5727-52d4-9a12-af3e4e3a4887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730137} {:answer/id #uuid "a636a947-141a-58ad-9a0a-db9efa3918cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a636a947-141a-58ad-9a0a-db9efa3918cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730138} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8a3677a-61f7-5090-92bf-2bc6c2961930" :answer-field/key "$x=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730179}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f2ec4d2-9f1a-59c8-aeba-911dc271f39d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73399" :question/problem "![](images/43/432991e403167bd560517072d24058c3f2106f093cdcad08f3b5f0ed486f9504.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively. \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that \n\n- at $x=3$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(3)=0,$ while\n\n- at $x=7$ there is a discontinuity, so  ${f}^{′}(7)$ doesn't exist.\n\n![](images/e0/e035d64e759108be78c54d0d8d1018906ef253bdcdaff548edd185b8b6543505.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two critical points, and their $x$-coordinates are $x=3$ and $x=7.$" :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186729440 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341964} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 37.998999999999995 :task-item/id #uuid "c9e913df-6481-4284-bf15-6fc79eee5170" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186729497} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "b45765bb-4323-55a3-9da0-49d